---
// Privacy policy for the new site. Replaces the 2020 notice from the old site,
// updated for the tools the new site actually uses (Zoho CRM enquiry form,
// Google Tag Manager with consent, Vercel hosting, Zoho invoice payment links).
// 4 Oct 2026: enquiry retention set to 3 months; Google Ads confirmed in use.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LegalStyles from '../components/LegalStyles.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | TMG Plumbing & Heating"
  description="How TMG Plumbing & Heating Services collects, uses and protects your personal information, and your rights under GDPR."
>
  <LegalStyles />
  <article class="legal mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated 4 October 2026</p>

    <p>
      TMG Plumbing &amp; Heating Services ("TMG", "we", "us") respects your privacy. This policy explains what
      personal information we collect when you use www.tmgplumbing.ie or ask us for a quote, how we use it, who we
      share it with, and the rights you have under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and the Irish Data
      Protection Acts.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      TMG Plumbing &amp; Heating Services, Unit 17F, Six Cross Roads Business Park, Waterford, X91 KV09, is the data
      controller for the personal information described in this policy. You can contact us about anything in it at
      <a href="mailto:info@tmgplumbing.ie">info@tmgplumbing.ie</a> or on 051 577 089.
    </p>

    <h2>2. What information we collect</h2>
    <h3>Information you give us</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>When you send an enquiry or ask for a quote: your name, phone number, email address, Eircode, company name
        (if any), the service you are asking about, any details you add and any photos you upload.</li>
      <li>When you phone, email or message us: whatever you choose to tell us.</li>
      <li>When we carry out work for you: the site address, details of your heating or plumbing system, and the
        records we need for quotes, invoices, reports and warranties.</li>
      <li>When you pay an invoice online: you pay through the secure payment link on your Zoho invoice. We receive
        confirmation of the payment, but we never see or store your full card details.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>If you accept analytics cookies: information about how you use the site, such as the pages you visit, the
        device and browser you use and roughly where you are (town or county level). See our
        <a href="/cookies-policy">Cookies Policy</a>.</li>
      <li>Our hosting provider keeps short-term technical logs (such as IP address and pages requested) to keep the
        site secure and working.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. How we use your information, and our legal basis</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>To reply to your enquiry and give you a quote</strong>: to take steps at your request before entering
        a contract.</li>
      <li><strong>To carry out and invoice the work, and honour guarantees</strong>: to perform our contract with you.</li>
      <li><strong>To keep business, tax and accounting records</strong>: to comply with our legal obligations.</li>
      <li><strong>To understand and improve how the website is used</strong>: your consent, given through the cookie
        banner.</li>
      <li><strong>To measure whether our online adverts (Google Ads) lead to enquiries</strong>: your consent, given
        through the cookie banner.</li>
      <li><strong>To send you service reminders or occasional news</strong>: your consent, or our legitimate interest
        in contacting existing customers about similar services. You can opt out at any time.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Who we share it with</h2>
    <p>We never sell your personal information. We share it only with service providers who help us run the business, under contracts that protect your data:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Zoho</strong> (EU data centre): stores enquiries and customer records, and provides the payment links on our invoices.</li>
      <li><strong>Google</strong> (Google Tag Manager, Google Analytics and Google Ads, only with your consent): website statistics and measuring our adverts.</li>
      <li><strong>LinkedIn</strong> (LinkedIn Insight Tag, only with your consent): measuring our adverts.</li>
      <li><strong>Vercel</strong>: hosts the website.</li>
      <li>Our accountants, insurers and professional advisers, and any subcontractor carrying out part of your job,
        where needed.</li>
      <li>Public authorities, where the law requires it.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Some of these providers may process data outside the European Economic Area. Where they do, they are
      covered by safeguards approved under GDPR, such as the European Commission's standard contractual clauses or
      the EU–US Data Privacy Framework.
    </p>

    <h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Enquiries that do not lead to work: three months, then deleted.</li>
      <li>Customer, job and invoice records: seven years after the work, as required for tax purposes, or longer if
        a guarantee or warranty is still running.</li>
      <li>Analytics data: up to fourteen months.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. How we keep it safe</h2>
    <p>
      We use reputable providers with strong security, limit access to the people who need it, and the website uses
      encrypted (HTTPS) connections. No system is completely secure, but we take reasonable steps to protect your
      information and will tell you and the Data Protection Commission about any serious breach as the law requires.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
    <p>Under GDPR you have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>ask for a copy of the personal information we hold about you;</li>
      <li>ask us to correct anything that is wrong or incomplete;</li>
      <li>ask us to delete your information, where we no longer need to keep it;</li>
      <li>ask us to limit how we use it, or object to us using it;</li>
      <li>ask for your information in a portable format;</li>
      <li>withdraw your consent at any time, for example by changing your
        <button type="button" data-open-cookie-settings class="underline text-orange">cookie settings</button>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To use any of these rights, email <a href="mailto:info@tmgplumbing.ie">info@tmgplumbing.ie</a>. We will reply
      within one month. If you are unhappy with how we have handled your information, you can complain to the
      Data Protection Commission at <a href="https://www.dataprotection.ie" rel="noopener">dataprotection.ie</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Children</h2>
    <p>Our services and website are intended for adults. We do not knowingly collect information from children.</p>

    <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top shows when it was last changed.</p>

    <h2>10. Contact us</h2>
    <p>
      TMG Plumbing &amp; Heating Services, Unit 17F, Six Cross Roads Business Park, Waterford, X91 KV09.<br />
      Email <a href="mailto:info@tmgplumbing.ie">info@tmgplumbing.ie</a> · Phone 051 577 089
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
